kind how-do-i
title How do I change the font set of a look?
intro A look's card lists its font set, size and color scheme. You change one on the card, and Esc keeps the change for Save.
see looks/make-a-look-and-use-it-on-the-console

file etc/vtium.conf
    version = 1
    font-name = unifont
    [look plain]
    palette = legacy
    [head console]
    vt = 5
    look = plain
file etc/batch.conf
    ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf
font fonts/mono.bdf 8x16
frit mono
    source=bdf:ROOT/fonts/mono.bdf

1. Go to the Looks tab.
2. Choose plain.
3. Choose Font set.
4. Choose mono.
at the card, before Esc
check screen shows "Esc keeps the changes"
check screen shows "Esc back, keep changes"
5. Press Esc.
6. Press s to save.
at the save
check draft look plain font-name mono
